{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"agent_message","text":"The required valid and explicit error matrices pass, but the generic FFI null audit exposes an important contract detail: C does not touch null filter pointers when the directive list is empty, while the Rust `main` currently decodes all filters eagerly. I’m correcting `main` to evaluate filters lazily in C’s short-circuit order, then adding subprocess signal comparisons for the pointer positions C actually dereferences and one-past scanner-width cases for every fixed field."}}
